# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# TOON store (Arweave DVM) box .env — copy to .env and fill in secrets.
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# Public domain (MUST match the DNS A-records for proxy.ario.* dvm.*)
DOMAIN=devnet.toonprotocol.dev

# Let's Encrypt — set to 0 for trusted prod certs (after DNS resolves)
LETSENCRYPT_STAGING=0
LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL=dev.jonathan.green@gmail.com

# ── SECRETS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BIP-39 mnemonic — the store-box connector + DVM derive all chain settlement
# keys + the DVM Nostr (kind:10032) identity from this.
#
# The value below is the well-known throwaway test phrase shipped by Hardhat and
# anvil. It is PUBLIC, it controls nothing, and it is here only so the file
# parses. Replace it in your own .env with a phrase you generated yourself.
#
# NEVER commit a real mnemonic — not to this file, not to any other. This file is
# tracked in a public repository; anything written here is published the moment it
# is pushed. Keep the real value in the box's untracked .env (see .gitignore) or
# in a secret manager, and rotate immediately if one ever lands in a commit.
TOON_MNEMONIC=test test test test test test test test test test test junk

LOG_LEVEL=info

# ── Rust parallel fleet (docker-compose.store.rust.yml only) ────────────────
# STORE_PEER_WIRE_BIND is GONE (ADR 0027, issue #679). It named the host
# interface the Rust connector's raw-TCP peer wire (4001) was published on;
# that wire is deleted, the overlay publishes one loopback-only port, and
# `docker compose ... -f docker-compose.store.rust.yml up` no longer reads
# any variable from this section. Peers now ride the carriages the client
# edge already serves, behind this box's existing nginx TLS front.
